From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:02:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: default UL MU-MIMO off and add live MURU
 flag control

Scheduled uplink triggers on MT798x can briefly pause best-effort
downlink traffic when either uplink MU flag is enabled. Previously
mimo_ul_en was unconditionally set on !MT7915, the AP always advertised
UL MU-MIMO in its HE PHY capabilities, and the firmware took the band
and BSS MURU flags from the first station record only, so changing them
needed a driver reload or a reboot.

- Add muru_mimo_ul (default off) and muru_ofdma_dl (default on) module
  parameters alongside muru_ofdma_ul (default off). muru_mimo_ul also
  gates IEEE80211_HE_PHY_CAP2_UL_MU_FULL_MU_MIMO; the capabilities
  follow it when the radio is set up, not the live control below.
- Stop sending muru->mimo_ul.partial_ul_mimo: the AP advertises
  full-bandwidth UL MU-MIMO only, so the firmware isn't told a station
  can do it in part of the channel.
- Add mt7915_mcu_set_muru_dl_ul() (MURU_CTRL subcmd 81) and send the
  flags for the band and the BSS on AP start, for the band and every AP
  and station BSS after a firmware restart, and through a new per-phy
  debugfs file (muru), so all four flags can be changed live per band.
  The band keeps DL MU-MIMO only while one of its APs MU beamforms;
  station interfaces don't count. A refused update is sent again by
  the next write. mimo_ul=1 is taken on the MT7915 but stays off there,
  so a line with all four flags still sets the other three.
- muru_unapplied is a plain bool, not a bit field next to
  restart_pending: it is written under the wiphy lock alone, and the
  reset work writes restart_pending without that lock.
- KUnit: STA_REC_MURU, HE capabilities, start_ap (another BSS keeping
  the band's DL MU-MIMO, a refused update), the band and BSS updates
  over every interface, restart recovery, parsing, and the debugfs
  file's read format and write.

Signed-off-by: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
